CHAPTER III
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
Article 4
Women and children victims of acts of violence receive the following rights: The right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected;
The right to health and psychological services for the suffering experienced by victims;
The right to legal assistance;
The right to obtain information;
The right to confidential handling;
The right to social rehabilitation;
The right to complaint handling;
The right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process; and Guarantee of rights related to status as members of the family and society.

